"""The shared database (schema `photos` of the shared Postgres, see strata-python's README, step 8): everything about the pictures that is not the pictures themselves. Needs strata-python[db] and pgvector (dependencies of the app); only the *_store modules import this package, and only when the database is switched on.

The `vector` extension lives in schema `public` of `omarchy`, but strata_python.db migrates with search_path set to the app's schema alone: a revision that creates a vector column first runs `SET LOCAL search_path TO photos, public` (see the initial one). At run time the URL should say `search_path=photos,public`."""
